---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const all = await getCollection('work');
const FAVOURITES = [
  'project-superorganism', 'out-of-the-loop', 'project-birds-of-australia',
  'platform-urbanism', 'project-we-dream-the-city',
];
const favourites = FAVOURITES
  .map(slug => all.find(w => w.id.replace(/\.md$/, '') === slug))
  .filter(Boolean);

const COMMITTEES = [
  { year: '2023–2025', name: 'Digital Advisory Committee', detail: 'State Library of Victoria' },
  { year: '2022–2024', name: 'Smart Cities Advisory Council', detail: 'City of Parramatta' },
  { year: '2021–2023', name: 'Product Council Asia Pacific, Co-Lead, Resilient Cities', detail: 'Urban Land Institute' },
  { year: '2021–2022', name: 'CEO Digital Advisor', detail: 'Australia Council / ACMI' },
  { year: '2013–2015', name: 'Board Member', detail: 'Dictionary of Sydney' },
];

const AWARDS = [
  { year: '2026', name: 'Commendation, Events, Exhibitions and Tours', detail: 'Birds of Australia STORYBOX. National Trust of Australia (NSW)' },
  { year: '2025', name: 'Digital Interpretation Award', detail: 'Birds of Australia STORYBOX with the Australian Museum. Interpretation Australia' },
  { year: '2025', name: 'Media Architecture Biennale Award, Participatory Media and Infrastructure', detail: 'STORYBOX' },
  { year: '2023', name: 'Heritage Award, Events, Exhibitions and Tours, Joint Winner', detail: 'Building Bridges Emu Projection. National Trust of Australia (NSW)' },
  { year: '2021', name: 'Digital Placemaking Award, Commendation', detail: 'STORYBOX, Asia Pacific Place Leaders Awards' },
  { year: '2020', name: 'Smart Cities Future of Place, Finalist', detail: 'Australia and NZ Smart Cities Council Awards' },
  { year: '2015', name: 'Outstanding Heritage Award, Winner', detail: "Mt Stromlo Director's Residence. National Trust ACT" },
  { year: '2008', name: 'Best Cross-Platform Content, Winner', detail: 'Sydney Sidetracks, ABC' },
];

const FELLOWSHIPS = [
  { year: '2023–2028', name: "Vice Chancellor's Senior Research Fellowship", detail: 'RMIT University, Centre for Urban Research' },
  { year: '2017', name: 'Museum of Arts and Science Research Fellowship', detail: '' },
  { year: '2015', name: 'Fellowship', detail: 'NYU Centre for Urban Science and Progress' },
  { year: '2014–2017', name: 'Postdoctoral Research Fellowship', detail: 'Urban Studies Foundation' },
  { year: '2006', name: 'Centre for Archival and Scholarly Research Fellowship', detail: 'National Film and Sound Archive' },
  { year: '2005–2009', name: 'Australian Postgraduate Award', detail: '' },
];

---

<Base
  title="About — Sarah Barns"
  banner={{
    src: 'https://pub-9840de99aef84197989ef35cf41fa967.r2.dev/docklands/docklands-water.mp4',
    captionTitle: 'Docklands Waterscape',
    captionBody: 'Wurundjuri lands, Naarm/Melbourne.',
  }}
>
  <div class="page-header about-header">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">I create, cultivate and write about digital interfaces and experiences as they shape relationships to places in transition. Methods: I write, I listen, I collaborate, I imagine.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose practice">
    <p>I'm a scholar-practitioner, specialising in collaborative, archive-led
      creative practice and the civic design of digital infrastructure. My work mostly spans
      cultural heritage interpretation, digital governance and urban technology.</p>

    <p class="practice-lead">While many urban technologists see the city as data, I see it as an
      archive of noisy events, voices, habitats and governing conditions.</p>

    <p>I deliberately straddle scholarship and collaborative practice, and lean heavily into live
      experimentation as strategy. I am particularly committed to ensuring the public record is one
      that future generations can continue to be inspired by and shape, with agency and purpose. By
      that I mean that we have digital archives and collections that are open and accessible as
      public goods, and inspire creative connections with the past. This focus has led to a long
      standing interest in how certain digital platforms can, by their design, limit access to
      shared digital resources and, over time, produce unhealthy knowledge practices. I wrote a book
      on this called
      <a href="https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-981-32-9725-8"><em>Platform Urbanism</em></a>
      (Palgrave, 2020) which examined the historical emergence of global platforms in shaping urban
      policy and infrastructure.</p>

    <p>My current research enquiry focuses on the collisions of AI sovereignties and citizen-AI
      activism in cities, and the governance protocols and pathways that underpin them. My
      disciplinary home is urban digital geography, specifically the historical and political
      geography of digital cities, but much of my practice is also creative and collaborative.</p>

    <p>Practice-wise I work with multidisciplinary teams to build and prototype helpful interfaces and story-lines that
      connect us to the places we live in and that sustain us. This work is funded through a range of
      partnerships and collaborations: research fellowships, start-up grants, project commissions,
      and self-funded and government R&amp;D.</p>

    <p>My key platforms are <a href="https://storybox.co">STORYBOX Places</a>,
      <a href="https://civicinterplay.io">Civic Interplay</a> and
      <a href="https://studioesem.com">Studio ESEM</a>, and I maintain a listening practice through
      <a href="https://soundcloud.com/soundwalking">Soundwalking</a>.</p>

    <p class="practice-intent">You can read my 2025 Manifesto <a href="/manifesto">here</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose longer">
    <h2 class="about-h2 longer-head">The longer story</h2>

    <p>I have come to an interest in digital cities out of a concern for what a 'data driven'
      approach leaves out. I come to an interest in archives in recognition that
      technology futures too often like to forget the past. So I try to make a habit of digging,
      retrieving and re-assembling.</p>

    <p>My PhD (2005&ndash;2010) used ambient sound archives to build mobile listening experiences that surfaced
      contested spatial histories, reimagining real-time city technologies as connection points to
      the real times of space. In 2008 that became <em>Sydney Sidetracks</em>, the ABC's first
      location-based service, which let people stand in Martin Place and hear it in 1945. I've
      continued to evolve my <a href="/listening">sound and listening practice</a> for the past
      fifteen years.</p>

    <p>In 2012 I negotiated the release of ABC television and radio archive material under Creative
      Commons, through a partnership with ABC Pool called Past Forward. Talbot Duckmanton reporting
      the end of the war, Juanita Nielsen on why she loved the Cross the year before she disappeared,
      Bea Miles, Chow Hayes, Wendy Bacon marking an eviction on Victoria Street.</p>

    <p>This practice continues: bringing data, stories, and archives into the open, whether under
      open licences or in shared spaces where they can be encountered in new ways.</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>Strategy and advisory</h2>

    <p>I work as a strategy adviser for selected organisations, building on my early career in policy
      and organisational change. I wrote the ABC's organisation-wide digital
      strategy and the Australia Council's first national creative industries strategy, and have
      delivered research and strategy for the Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet through
      Data61, UCL's Institute for Innovation and Public Purpose, Create NSW, the NSW Government
      Architect and the Australian Museum. Some of my strategy projects can be explored
      <a href="/strategy">here</a>.</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>Studio ESEM and STORYBOX Places</h2>

    <p>With my creative and life partner Michael Killalea I founded Esem Projects in 2013. This began
      as a creative idea, and turned into a studio practice running for over a decade. We rebranded as
      <a href="https://studioesem.com">Studio ESEM</a> in 2023, using creative and experiential design
      methods to bring to life the stories that shape places through time. Partners and clients
      include the Australian Museum, the ABC, HASSELL, the NSW Government Architect and many local
      government agencies.</p>

    <p>In 2020 we developed <a href="https://storybox.co">STORYBOX Places</a> as participatory digital
      infrastructure, and have since delivered over forty digital placemaking programs through this
      initiative.</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>Civic AI research</h2>

    <p>My current enquiry is the collision of AI sovereignties with citizen-AI activism in cities, and
      the governance protocols that underpin them. It follows on from my book
      <a href="https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-981-32-9725-8"><em>Platform Urbanism</em></a>
      (Palgrave Macmillan, 2019), which examined the rise of platform business models as an emergent
      governance infrastructure for cities, and helped to shape a lively field of digital geography
      (Google Scholar citations c2026, 700+).</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>Golden threads</h2>

    <p>Running through the scholarship, the studio practice and the writing is what I think of as a
      long-form narrative inquiry into how digital systems reshape place, citizenship and collective
      governance. Golden threads structuring space through time, resisting what Jameson once called 'the actuarial
      colonisation of the unknown'. I am writing a book about it, <em>Still Here</em>, structured as a
      topographical excavation of sites through modes of encounter: listening, reading, installing,
      diagnosing, gathering, letting go.</p>

    <p>I am based in Sydney. Outside of work I keep a body-based practice through Pilates, yoga,
      cycling and dance, and a long-standing interest in deep-time writing as a counterweight to the
      accelerationist logics of the systems I study.</p>

    <p class="closing-line">Perhaps this can all be put simply: how we draw the lines that shape the
      spines that carry our lives, briefly, on this earth awhile.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="affiliations">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Current positions</h2>
    <div class="affiliation">
      <div class="affiliation-role">Vice Chancellor's Senior Research Fellow</div>
      <div class="affiliation-org"><a href="https://www.rmit.edu.au/profiles/b/sarah-barns2">RMIT University</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="affiliation">
      <div class="affiliation-role">Founder &amp; Director</div>
      <div class="affiliation-org"><a href="https://studioesem.com">Studio ESEM</a> (est. 2011)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="affiliation">
      <div class="affiliation-role">Creator</div>
      <div class="affiliation-org"><a href="https://storybox.co">STORYBOX</a> &middot; <a href="https://civicinterplay.io">Civic Interplay</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Profiles</h2>
    <p class="profile-links">
      <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0087-7166">ORCID</a>
      <span class="sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Sarah-Barns-4">ResearchGate</a>
      <span class="sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=cnGxyWQAAAAJ&amp;hl=en">Google Scholar</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">My favourite personal work</h2>
    {favourites.map(w => (
      <div class="pub-item">
        <div class="pub-title">
          {w.data.href ? <a href={w.data.href} rel="noopener">{w.data.title}</a> : w.data.title}
        </div>
        <div class="pub-details">{w.data.venue}, {w.data.yearLabel ?? w.data.year}</div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Previous positions</h2>
    <p class="prev-roles">
      Before RMIT I held an Industry Fellowship at the QUT Design Lab and a Visiting Fellowship at the
      Melbourne Centre for Cities (2021&ndash;22), and before that was Engaged Research Fellow
      (2018&ndash;19) and Urban Studies Foundation Postdoctoral Research Fellow (2014&ndash;17) at the
      Institute for Culture and Society, Western Sydney University.
    </p>
    <p class="prev-roles">
      I co-directed Esem Projects from 2013 to 2022. My previous roles have included Manager of
      Strategic Initiatives at the UTS Creative Industries Innovation Centre, Smart Cities SME at
      CSIRO/Data61, Senior Consultant in Urban Informatics at Arup, and Digital R&amp;D Lead at ABC
      New Media.
    </p>
    <p class="prev-roles">
      My career began in public policy in 2000, with roles across the Department of Communications,
      the media and telecommunications think-tank Network Insight, the Australian Communications and
      Media Authority, the Australia Council for the Arts and the ABC.
    </p>
    <div class="honour">
      <span class="honour-year">2005&ndash;2010</span>
      <span class="honour-body">
        <span class="honour-name">Doctor of Philosophy</span>
        <span class="honour-detail">University of Technology Sydney</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="honour">
      <span class="honour-year">1993&ndash;1998</span>
      <span class="honour-body">
        <span class="honour-name">Bachelor of Arts (First Class Honours), Politics &amp; International Relations</span>
        <span class="honour-detail">Murdoch University</span>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Awards</h2>
    {AWARDS.map(a => (
      <div class="honour">
        <span class="honour-year">{a.year}</span>
        <span class="honour-body">
          <span class="honour-name">{a.name}</span>
          {a.detail && <span class="honour-detail">{a.detail}</span>}
        </span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Fellowships</h2>
    {FELLOWSHIPS.map(a => (
      <div class="honour">
        <span class="honour-year">{a.year}</span>
        <span class="honour-body">
          <span class="honour-name">{a.name}</span>
          {a.detail && <span class="honour-detail">{a.detail}</span>}
        </span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="publications">
    <h2 class="about-h2">Committees &amp; memberships</h2>
    {COMMITTEES.map(c => (
      <div class="honour">
        <span class="honour-year">{c.year}</span>
        <span class="honour-body">
          <span class="honour-name">{c.name}</span>
          {c.detail && <span class="honour-detail">{c.detail}</span>}
        </span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

</Base>

<style>
  /* About — elevated into the shared design language (scoped to this page) */
  .about-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3rem); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .about-header .page-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--body); font-style: italic; font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.9vw, 1.25rem); color: var(--text-dim); line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 48ch;
  }
  /* Lead paragraph */
  .prose > p:first-of-type { color: var(--text); }
  .prose > p:first-of-type strong { font-weight: 500; }
  /* Section headings in the display face */
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.75rem); letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  /* Section headings sit in the same display face as the prose h2s above them,
     so the page reads as one hierarchy rather than two competing label styles. */
  .about-h2 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.75rem); letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    line-height: 1.2; color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }
  .affiliation-org a {
    color: var(--text-dim); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember-ink) 35%, transparent);
  }
  .affiliation-org a:hover { color: var(--text); text-decoration-color: var(--ember-ink); }
  .profile-links {
    font-family: var(--heading); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-faint);
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.55rem; align-items: center;
  }
  .profile-links a {
    color: var(--ember-ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember-ink) 35%, transparent);
  }
  .profile-links a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--ember-ink); }
  .profile-links .sep { color: var(--text-faint); }
  .pub-title a {
    color: var(--text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember-ink) 38%, transparent);
    transition: text-decoration-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .pub-title a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--ember-ink); }
  /* Works still awaiting a URL — render as plain text, not a dead link */
  .pub-title a[data-needs-url] { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; pointer-events: none; }
  .practice > p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .practice-lead {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.62; color: var(--text); max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1.6rem; padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--ember-ink);
  }
  .practice-intent {
    font-family: var(--display); line-height: 1.62;
    color: var(--text); max-width: 48ch; margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }
  .closing-line {
    font-family: var(--display); font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text); max-width: 46ch;
    margin-top: 2.4rem; padding-top: 1.6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .longer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .longer-head { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .prev-roles {
    line-height: 1.62; color: var(--text-dim);
    max-width: 66ch; margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .honour {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 1fr; gap: 0.4rem 1rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .honour-year {
    font-family: var(--heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--text-faint); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .honour-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.12rem; }
  .honour-name { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.35; }
  .honour-detail { font-family: var(--heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 300; color: var(--text-dim); }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .honour { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

</style>
